From f874915e6e47f3098adc29b1e2eeea46b57d7c6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] validation: resolve batch inputs in one wave using PeekCoin

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Resolve intra-batch and confirmed inputs in a single pass using the flat
open-addressed txid_table and CCoinsViewCache::PeekCoin, and link mempool
parent iterators in O(1).

Original-Commit: 2e1bd9c9d007e29db509bb92d0b3da0face7da0f
Original-Patch: ecash/039
Split-Concern: inputs

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Preserve flat one-wave input resolution/PeekCoin and reuse the resolved coins for notifications. Keep previously validated all-or-nothing capacity reservation and parallel standard/actual-consensus script checks instead of routing raw batches through limit-trimming SubmitPackage. Parent-iterator insertion APIs belong to next61 with their actual mempool implementation; fields are retained here as resolution metadata, and the lookup-skipping consumer is tracked there.

